So the filelist filter probes data that looks like a playlist (lines of URLs). The playlist can contain a `satip://` URL. When the filelist filter processes the playlist, it loads each URL as a source. If a URL is `satip://...`, the rtpin filter is used with `ctx->src` set to that URL.

So the PoC is a playlist file containing a `satip://` URL with a very long server name. Let me verify the flow:
1. Input file is a playlist (e.g., one line: `satip://AAAA...`)
2. The filelist filter (`flist`) probes it as a playlist
3. The filelist filter loads the `satip://` URL as a source
4. The rtpin filter is instantiated with `src=satip://AAAA...`
5. `rtpin_initialize` calls `rtpin_satip_get_server_ip` which overflows `text[1024]`

Let me check the filelist filter's probe score and how it loads URLs. Let me also verify the exact overflow condition.

The overflow in `rtpin_satip_get_server_ip`:
```c
char text[1024];
...
//get the server name
is_ipv6 = GF_FALSE;
len = (u32)strlen(test);
i = 0;
while (i<len) {
    if (test[i] == '[') is_ipv6 = GF_TRUE;
    else if (test[i] == ']') is_ipv6 = GF_FALSE;
    if ((test[i] == '/') || (!is_ipv6 && (test[i] == ':'))) break;
    text[i] = test[i];
    i += 1;
}
text[i] = 0;
```

`test` points to `sURL + 6` (after `satip://`). The loop copies characters until `/` or `:` (when not in IPv6 brackets). If the server name is longer than 1024 chars, `text` overflows.

So the PoC should be a playlist with a line like:
```
satip://AAAA...AAAA
```
where the server name (after `satip://`) is > 1024 characters.

But wait - I need to check if the filelist filter actually loads the URL. Let me check how the filelist filter processes the playlist and loads sources.

